id=a52sxq_resolution_fingerprint
name=Galaxy A52s 5G: fingerprint touch area stays on the sensor when booting in HD+ / 540p
author=kusti420
description=UNTESTED-ON-DEVICE. Follow-up to resolution_scaling. system_server's SemUdfpsHelper.fetchDisplayInfo() computes the panel's native dpi as maxWidth / (Display.getMode().getPhysicalWidth() / DisplayMetrics.xdpi), assuming xdpi belongs to the active mode's pixel grid. With resolution_scaling xdpi belongs to the forced (logical) grid (272.95 at HD+, 204.72 at 540p) while the mode stays 1080 wide, so when system_server STARTS in HD+ / 540p the FOD rectangle sent to the touch IC (set_fod_rect, native panel pixels, computed once per boot) is 2/3 or 1/2 size and 5.4 / 8.1 mm too low: (460,2144)-(619,2303) or (480,2208)-(599,2327) instead of (420,2017)-(658,2255). The width that pairs with xdpi is now the display's natural (logical) width. Also: BiometricSetting's LightSourceView only recomputed the optical light disc position on a rotation change; it now does so every time the light is switched on, so a resolution switch during a live fingerprint session cannot leave the disc at the old pixel position.
